      "message": "LOGS_DIR\u003d\"$(cd .../logs \u0026\u0026 pwd)\" is empty when ../logs doesn’t exist (set -u doesn’t catch an empty value), so rm -rf $LOGS_DIR/* becomes rm -rf /*. Abort if the directory is missing, quote the variable, and use \"${LOGS_DIR:?}\"/*. Wiping is also on by default and deletes everyone’s logs in the shared folder; make it opt-in",
